  "riskClass": "medium",
  "title": "VariantManager uses response.ok-style check on safeJson result instead of response.ok",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: Wiring. Severity: P2. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. In loadVariants(), the code does `const data = await safeJson(res);` then checks `if (data?.ok)`. The safeJson utility returns the raw JSON body from the response, NOT a parsed result with an `.ok` property. The `.ok` property would only exist if the API response body itself contains an `ok` field. If the API returns `{ data: [...] }` without an explicit `ok` field, data?.ok evaluates to undefined/falsy, causing the 'Failed to load variants' error even on successful responses. Similar pattern appears in handleAdd (line 126) and handleUpdate (line 178).",
